window.TL = {"duration": 450.59, "scenes": [{"id": "s1", "label": "Opening & Key Takeaway", "start": 0, "end": 42.08}, {"id": "s2", "label": "01. Korean Workbook Market and Competitive Landscape", "start": 42.08, "end": 109.07}, {"id": "s3", "label": "02. JEI's Strengths and Current Limitations", "start": 109.07, "end": 175.49}, {"id": "s4", "label": "03. Parents' Needs and Primary Target Customers", "start": 175.49, "end": 240.55}, {"id": "s5", "label": "04. Core Differentiation: From Assessment to Visible Growth", "start": 240.55, "end": 296.07}, {"id": "s6", "label": "05. Proposed Brand Positioning and Customer Messaging", "start": 296.07, "end": 371.2}, {"id": "s7", "label": "06. Service Development and Operational Directions", "start": 371.2, "end": 424.56}, {"id": "s8", "label": "Closing", "start": 424.56, "end": 450.59}], "cont": ["s1", "s2", "s3", "s4", "s5", "s6", "s7", "s8"], "order": ["l1_1", "l1_2", "l1_3", "l1_4", "l1_5", "l2_1", "l2_2", "l2_3", "l2_4", "l2_5", "l2_6", "l2_7", "l2_8", "l2_9", "l3_1", "l3_2", "l3_3", "l3_4", "l3_5", "l3_6", "l3_7", "l3_8", "l3_9", "l4_1", "l4_2", "l4_3", "l4_4", "l4_5", "l4_6", "l4_7", "l4_8", "l4_9", "l5_1", "l5_2", "l5_3", "l5_4", "l5_5", "l5_6", "l5_7", "l5_8", "l5_9", "l6_1", "l6_2", "l6_3", "l6_4", "l6_5", "l6_6", "l6_7", "l6_8", "l6_9", "l6_10", "l6_11", "l6_12", "l6_13", "l7_1", "l7_2", "l7_3", "l7_4", "l7_5", "l7_6", "l7_7", "l7_8", "l8_1", "l8_2", "l8_3", "l8_4", "l8_5"], "lines": {"l1_1": {"scene": "s1", "text": "Today, I will present JEI's repositioning strategy for the Korean market.", "start": 0.6, "end": 5.49, "words": [["today", 0.36], ["i", 1.16], ["will", 1.18], ["present", 1.36], ["jei's", 1.78], ["repositioning", 2.88], ["strategy", 3.74], ["for", 4.12], ["the", 4.48], ["korean", 4.58], ["market", 4.88]]}, "l1_2": {"scene": "s1", "text": "Our key message to customers is clear.", "start": 6.19, "end": 8.7, "words": [["our", 6.06], ["key", 6.42], ["message", 6.6], ["to", 6.96], ["customers", 7.22], ["is", 7.64], ["clear", 8.1]]}, "l1_3": {"scene": "s1", "text": "JEI can differentiate itself by using precise diagnosis and assessment to design the learning path each child needs, and by helping children develop the ability to grow independently.", "start": 9.4, "end": 20.69, "words": []}, "l1_4": {"scene": "s1", "text": "To deliver on that promise, we must connect our diagnostic results to each child's actual learning experience and show parents clear evidence of progress.", "start": 21.39, "end": 30.7, "words": []}, "l1_5": {"scene": "s1", "text": "I'll begin with the competitive landscape, then discuss JEI's strengths and limitations, what parents need, our proposed brand positioning, and the steps needed to deliver it.", "start": 31.4, "end": 41.53, "words": []}, "l2_1": {"scene": "s2", "text": "The Korean workbook market has become more competitive, with traditional providers offering increasingly different learning models.", "start": 42.98, "end": 49.98, "words": []}, "l2_2": {"scene": "s2", "text": "Competition now extends beyond workbook providers to local study rooms, private learning centers, and digital learning programs.", "start": 50.68, "end": 58.3, "words": []}, "l2_3": {"scene": "s2", "text": "The four major workbook providers in Korea have different business models and strategies.", "start": 59.0, "end": 64.09, "words": []}, "l2_4": {"scene": "s2", "text": "Daekyo operates learning spaces such as Learning Centers and Hi CAMPUS, and offers learning content through its Summit program.", "start": 64.79, "end": 72.26, "words": []}, "l2_5": {"scene": "s2", "text": "Kumon records students' handwritten work digitally and supports learning between home visits through Daily Care.", "start": 72.96, "end": 79.19, "words": []}, "l2_6": {"scene": "s2", "text": "Woongjin combines learning across all subjects with AI features through its Smart All program.", "start": 79.89, "end": 85.67, "words": []}, "l2_7": {"scene": "s2", "text": "JEI's strengths include paper-based learning, individualized learning paths, precise assessment, and instructor coaching.", "start": 86.37, "end": 93.6, "words": []}, "l2_8": {"scene": "s2", "text": "Among these competitors, Kumon is our most direct competitor because we both focus on paper-based learning and home visits.", "start": 94.3, "end": 101.61, "words": []}, "l2_9": {"scene": "s2", "text": "Therefore, JEI needs to clearly show how we design learning for each child based on assessment results.", "start": 102.31, "end": 108.52, "words": []}, "l3_1": {"scene": "s3", "text": "JEI has five key strengths: precise diagnostic assessment, learning at each child's own pace, step-by-step workbooks, paper-based learning, and instructor coaching.", "start": 109.97, "end": 120.05, "words": []}, "l3_2": {"scene": "s3", "text": "We also have a long history and a strong reputation for quality learning materials.", "start": 120.75, "end": 125.69, "words": []}, "l3_3": {"scene": "s3", "text": "However, parents now have many learning options, including AI and digital programs.", "start": 126.39, "end": 131.41, "words": []}, "l3_4": {"scene": "s3", "text": "So, we need to give parents a clear reason to choose JEI.", "start": 132.11, "end": 136.15, "words": []}, "l3_5": {"scene": "s3", "text": "The problem we want to solve is that assessment results do not always lead to the right learning materials, starting level, or learning pace for each child.", "start": 136.85, "end": 145.8, "words": []}, "l3_6": {"scene": "s3", "text": "Even at JEI Learning Centers, if we assess students only when they first join, or only tell parents how far their child has progressed, parents may still have questions.", "start": 146.5, "end": 156.19, "words": []}, "l3_7": {"scene": "s3", "text": "Assessment results should lead to real changes in each child's learning.", "start": 156.89, "end": 161.3, "words": []}, "l3_8": {"scene": "s3", "text": "We also need to show parents how these changes help their children improve.", "start": 162.0, "end": 166.19, "words": []}, "l3_9": {"scene": "s3", "text": "Simply emphasizing self-learning, personalized learning, or AI is not enough to differentiate JEI from competitors.", "start": 166.89, "end": 174.94, "words": []}, "l4_1": {"scene": "s4", "text": "The first question parents ask is, \"Where is my child having difficulty, and what should my child learn first?\"", "start": 176.39, "end": 182.92, "words": []}, "l4_2": {"scene": "s4", "text": "When sharing assessment results, we should also explain which subject and level their child should start with, as well as the most appropriate learning pace.", "start": 183.62, "end": 191.98, "words": []}, "l4_3": {"scene": "s4", "text": "Parents also want their children to study independently, without constant reminders.", "start": 192.68, "end": 197.5, "words": []}, "l4_4": {"scene": "s4", "text": "Once learning begins, short assignments and instructors' encouragement help children keep studying every day.", "start": 198.2, "end": 204.56, "words": []}, "l4_5": {"scene": "s4", "text": "Over time, progress reports should show parents what their child can now do on their own and what they will learn next.", "start": 205.26, "end": 212.29, "words": []}, "l4_6": {"scene": "s4", "text": "Our first priority is parents of children in Grades 1 to 4 who want to understand where their child is having difficulty.", "start": 212.99, "end": 220.22, "words": []}, "l4_7": {"scene": "s4", "text": "For Grades 1 and 2, we focus on building regular study habits and independent learning skills.", "start": 220.92, "end": 226.74, "words": []}, "l4_8": {"scene": "s4", "text": "For Grades 2 to 4, we focus on identifying learning gaps and areas of difficulty.", "start": 227.44, "end": 232.52, "words": []}, "l4_9": {"scene": "s4", "text": "Seven-year-olds preparing for elementary school and students in Grades 5 and 6 are also important target groups.", "start": 233.22, "end": 240.0, "words": []}, "l5_1": {"scene": "s5", "text": "Our key differentiation is not simply better grading.", "start": 241.45, "end": 244.65, "words": []}, "l5_2": {"scene": "s5", "text": "It is how we connect assessment results to individualized learning and make each child's progress visible.", "start": 245.35, "end": 251.69, "words": []}, "l5_3": {"scene": "s5", "text": "We use assessment to find where each child needs help.", "start": 252.39, "end": 255.56, "words": []}, "l5_4": {"scene": "s5", "text": "Based on the results, we select appropriate workbooks, determine the starting level, and design an individualized learning path.", "start": 256.26, "end": 263.89, "words": []}, "l5_5": {"scene": "s5", "text": "Instructors check their work, coach them where needed, and adjust their learning pace.", "start": 264.59, "end": 269.63, "words": []}, "l5_6": {"scene": "s5", "text": "Then, we assess students again and use progress reports to see what has changed and set the next learning goal.", "start": 270.33, "end": 276.65, "words": []}, "l5_7": {"scene": "s5", "text": "This is how we connect assessment, individualized learning, and instructor coaching to each child's actual progress.", "start": 277.35, "end": 284.37, "words": []}, "l5_8": {"scene": "s5", "text": "Progress reports should not simply present information in a better format.", "start": 285.07, "end": 289.38, "words": []}, "l5_9": {"scene": "s5", "text": "They should provide clear evidence of how our learning system works and how children are improving.", "start": 290.08, "end": 295.52, "words": []}, "l6_1": {"scene": "s6", "text": "JEI aims to be a brand that helps children build the ability to grow on their own through precise assessment and personalized learning paths designed for each child.", "start": 296.97, "end": 306.74, "words": []}, "l6_2": {"scene": "s6", "text": "For parents, precise assessment is a reason to choose JEI.", "start": 307.44, "end": 311.95, "words": []}, "l6_3": {"scene": "s6", "text": "The core of our service is using assessment results to choose the right learning materials and learning sequence for each child.", "start": 312.65, "end": 319.56, "words": []}, "l6_4": {"scene": "s6", "text": "Our goal is to help children understand more and solve more problems on their own.", "start": 320.26, "end": 325.04, "words": []}, "l6_5": {"scene": "s6", "text": "This is based on JEI's philosophy:", "start": 325.74, "end": 328.31, "words": []}, "l6_6": {"scene": "s6", "text": "\"We believe in the power of self-learning.\"", "start": 329.01, "end": 331.3, "words": []}, "l6_7": {"scene": "s6", "text": "Our message to customers is:", "start": 332.0, "end": 333.75, "words": []}, "l6_8": {"scene": "s6", "text": "\"What your child needs to learn. The power to learn independently.\"", "start": 334.45, "end": 338.3, "words": []}, "l6_9": {"scene": "s6", "text": "We can explain this message in one sentence:", "start": 339.0, "end": 341.54, "words": []}, "l6_10": {"scene": "s6", "text": "\"Start with a precise assessment and focus on what your child needs to learn now.\"", "start": 342.24, "end": 346.82, "words": []}, "l6_11": {"scene": "s6", "text": "In our advertising and on our website, we will show how we check each child's level and help them learn step by step in the right order.", "start": 347.52, "end": 355.29, "words": []}, "l6_12": {"scene": "s6", "text": "When meeting with parents, we will start by asking, \"What should your child learn first?\"", "start": 355.99, "end": 361.14, "words": []}, "l6_13": {"scene": "s6", "text": "Rather than simply promoting personalized learning or AI features, we need to show parents what their child needs to learn and how their child is improving.", "start": 361.84, "end": 370.65, "words": []}, "l7_1": {"scene": "s7", "text": "We need to connect JEI's strengths in assessment and learning management across subjects.", "start": 372.1, "end": 377.45, "words": []}, "l7_2": {"scene": "s7", "text": "First, we will set clear standards for assessment and learning plans.", "start": 378.15, "end": 382.29, "words": []}, "l7_3": {"scene": "s7", "text": "Then, we will expand from Math to Korean and English.", "start": 382.74, "end": 386.2, "words": []}, "l7_4": {"scene": "s7", "text": "Second, we will connect paper-based learning and instructor coaching with digital progress reports.", "start": 386.9, "end": 392.59, "words": []}, "l7_5": {"scene": "s7", "text": "These reports should help parents track their child's progress through mobile apps and parent consultations.", "start": 393.29, "end": 399.94, "words": []}, "l7_6": {"scene": "s7", "text": "We can also explore how our Learning Centers and personalized POD workbooks could work together.", "start": 400.64, "end": 406.52, "words": []}, "l7_7": {"scene": "s7", "text": "In addition, we need to focus not only on new enrollment but also on student retention, the number of subjects per member, and revenue per customer.", "start": 407.22, "end": 415.7, "words": []}, "l7_8": {"scene": "s7", "text": "We will check our results using enrollment rates after assessment, reassessment rates, report viewing rates, and retention rates.", "start": 416.4, "end": 424.01, "words": []}, "l8_1": {"scene": "s8", "text": "In the end, parents should be able to explain how their child's learning has changed and what the next learning goal is.", "start": 425.46, "end": 432.2, "words": []}, "l8_2": {"scene": "s8", "text": "Our goal is to connect precise assessment, individualized learning, and instructor coaching, and make each child's progress visible to parents.", "start": 432.9, "end": 441.36, "words": []}, "l8_3": {"scene": "s8", "text": "This is the reason we want parents to choose JEI.", "start": 442.06, "end": 445.36, "words": []}, "l8_4": {"scene": "s8", "text": "This concludes my presentation.", "start": 446.06, "end": 448.03, "words": []}, "l8_5": {"scene": "s8", "text": "Thank you.", "start": 448.73, "end": 449.39, "words": []}}};
